Algorithm: Circular Linked List for Coach Management

Step 1: Start the program.
Step 2: Initialize an empty circular linked list by setting last = NULL.
Step 3: Display the menu containing the following operations:
• Add a coach
• Remove a coach
• Display all coaches
• Exit
Step 4: Accept the user's choice.
Step 5: If the user selects Add Coach:
• Create a new node.
• Enter the coach number.
• If the list is empty, point the new node to itself.
• Otherwise, insert the new coach at the end and update the circular connection.
Step 6: If the user selects Remove Coach:
• Enter the coach number to remove.
• Search for the coach in the list.
• If found, delete the node and update the links.
• If not found, display an appropriate message.
Step 7: If the user selects Display Coaches, traverse the circular linked list and display all
coach numbers.
Step 8: Repeat Steps 3–7 until the user selects Exit.
Step 9: Release the allocated memory and stop the program.
— End of Algorithm —
